## Release vm.args — extends the default mix release template with Erlang
## distribution bound to loopback (research.md §R11/§R12), so the node is
## reachable only via `docker exec ... bin/speckit_orchestrator remote`
## (FR-025), never over the container's network interface.
##
## ${RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION}/${RELEASE_NODE}/${RELEASE_COOKIE} are substituted at
## boot by the release's env.sh from the identically-named env vars — see
## https://hexdocs.pm/mix/Mix.Tasks.Release.html#module-vm-args-and-environment-variables
##
## (No explicit -mode here: the release runner script already passes
## `--erl "-mode $RELEASE_MODE"` unconditionally, so one here would just be a
## harmless-but-noisy duplicate.)

-${RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION} ${RELEASE_NODE}
-setcookie ${RELEASE_COOKIE}

-kernel inet_dist_use_interface '{127,0,0,1}'
